{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Lebanon.</b> There is no need for the word 'burnt offerings,' for Lebanon is insufficient for burning. The sense of 'Lebanon' is so that the hearers will understand, for the meaning is all the trees of the earth; likewise the sense of 'its beasts.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:06.374731203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}